        {"id":"d_pi","sk":"piatok","en":"Friday","g":"m"},
        {"id":"d_so","sk":"sobota","en":"Saturday","g":"f"},
        {"id":"d_ne","sk":"nedeľa","en":"Sunday","g":"f"},
        {"id":"p_kolkojehodin","sk":"Koľko je hodín?","en":"What time is it?"},
        {"id":"p_vidimesa","sk":"Vidíme sa zajtra.","en":"See you tomorrow."},
        {"id":"p_mascas","sk":"Máš čas?","en":"Do you have time? (informal)"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "u9",
      "stage": "survival",
      "title": "Vonku · Out and about",
      "intro": "Enough to get around a Slovak town, order in a café and pay. In shops, always greet with <b>Dobrý deň</b> when you walk in.",
      "items": [
        {"id":"p_zachod","sk":"Kde je záchod?","en":"Where is the toilet?","alt":["Kde je toaleta?"]},
        {"id":"p_kdestanica","sk":"Kde je stanica?","en":"Where is the station?"},
        {"id":"w_obchod","sk":"obchod","en":"shop","g":"m"},
        {"id":"w_lekaren","sk":"lekáreň","en":"pharmacy","g":"f"},
        {"id":"w_stanica","sk":"stanica","en":"station","g":"f"},
        {"id":"w_vlak","sk":"vlak","en":"train","g":"m"},
        {"id":"w_autobus","sk":"autobus","en":"bus","g":"m"},
        {"id":"w_letisko","sk":"letisko","en":"airport","g":"n"},
        {"id":"w_ulica","sk":"ulica","en":"street","g":"f"},
        {"id":"w_vlavo","sk":"vľavo","en":"(on the) left"},
        {"id":"w_vpravo","sk":"vpravo","en":"(on the) right"},
        {"id":"w_rovno","sk":"rovno","en":"straight ahead"},
        {"id":"p_ucet","sk":"Účet, prosím.","en":"The bill, please."},
        {"id":"p_kartou","sk":"Môžem platiť kartou?","en":"Can I pay by card?"},
        {"id":"p_pomoc","sk":"Pomoc!","en":"Help!"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g1",
      "stage": "grammar",
      "title": "Byť · To be",
      "intro": "The most important verb. Slovak usually drops the pronoun, because the verb already says who: <b>Som doma</b> means \"I'm at home\".<table><tr><td>ja</td><td><b>som</b></td><td>I am</td></tr><tr><td>ty</td><td><b>si</b></td><td>you are</td></tr><tr><td>on / ona / ono</td><td><b>je</b></td><td>he / she / it is</td></tr><tr><td>my</td><td><b>sme</b></td><td>we are</td></tr><tr><td>vy</td><td><b>ste</b></td><td>you are (formal / plural)</td></tr><tr><td>oni</td><td><b>sú</b></td><td>they are</td></tr></table>Negative: put <b>nie</b> in front, as a separate word: <b>nie som</b>, <b>nie je</b>.",
      "items": [
        {"id":"g1_som","sk":"Ja som lekárka.","en":"I am a doctor. (woman)","blank":"som","choices":["som","si","je"]},
        {"id":"g1_si","sk":"Ty si môj priateľ.","en":"You are my boyfriend.","blank":"si","choices":["som","si","je"]},
        {"id":"g1_je","sk":"On je zo Slovenska.","en":"He is from Slovakia.","blank":"je","choices":["je","sú","si"]},
        {"id":"g1_ona","sk":"Ona je Američanka.","en":"She is American.","blank":"je","choices":["som","je","sú"]},
        {"id":"g1_sme","sk":"My sme spolu.","en":"We are together.","blank":"sme","choices":["sme","ste","sú"]},
        {"id":"g1_ste","sk":"Vy ste z Bratislavy?","en":"Are you from Bratislava? (formal)","blank":"ste","choices":["sme","ste","sú"]},
        {"id":"g1_su","sk":"Oni sú doma.","en":"They are at home.","blank":"sú","choices":["je","sme","sú"]},
        {"id":"g1_niesom","sk":"Nie som hladná.","en":"I'm not hungry. (woman)","blank":"Nie som","choices":["Nie som","Nesom","Som nie"]},
        {"id":"g1_nieje","sk":"To nie je problém.","en":"That's not a problem.","blank":"nie je","choices":["nie je","neje","je nie"]},
        {"id":"g1_kdeste","sk":"Kde ste?","en":"Where are you? (formal / plural)","blank":"ste","choices":["si","ste","sú"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g2",
      "stage": "grammar",
      "title": "Ten, tá, to · Gender in action",
      "intro": "Words that describe a noun take its gender. Masculine words end in <b>-ý</b>, feminine in <b>-á</b>, neuter in <b>-é</b>. \"That/the\" works the same way.<table><tr><td><span class=\"g g-m\">m</span></td><td><b>ten</b> dobr<b>ý</b> brat</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"g g-f\">f</span></td><td><b>tá</b> dobr<b>á</b> sestra</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"g g-n\">n</span></td><td><b>to</b> dobr<b>é</b> pivo</td></tr></table>\"My\" follows the same pattern: <b>môj</b>, <b>moja</b>, <b>moje</b>.",
      "items": [
        {"id":"g2_dom","sk":"ten veľký dom","en":"the big house","blank":"veľký","choices":["veľký","veľká","veľké"]},
        {"id":"g2_izba","sk":"tá malá izba","en":"the small room","blank":"malá","choices":["malý","malá","malé"]},
        {"id":"g2_pivo","sk":"to dobré pivo","en":"the good beer","blank":"dobré","choices":["dobrý","dobrá","dobré"]},
        {"id":"g2_kava","sk":"Káva je horúca.","en":"The coffee is hot.","blank":"horúca","choices":["horúci","horúca","horúce"]},
        {"id":"g2_polievka","sk":"Polievka je výborná.","en":"The soup is excellent.","blank":"výborná","choices":["výborný","výborná","výborné"]},
        {"id":"g2_film","sk":"Ten film je dobrý.","en":"That movie is good.","blank":"Ten","choices":["Ten","Tá","To"]},
        {"id":"g2_kniha","sk":"Tá kniha je zaujímavá.","en":"That book is interesting.","blank":"Tá","choices":["Ten","Tá","To"]},
        {"id":"g2_mesto","sk":"To mesto je krásne.","en":"That town is beautiful.","blank":"To","choices":["Ten","Tá","To"]},
        {"id":"g2_otec","sk":"Môj otec je vysoký.","en":"My father is tall.","blank":"vysoký","choices":["vysoký","vysoká","vysoké"]},
        {"id":"g2_mama","sk":"Moja mama je milá.","en":"My mom is nice.","blank":"Moja","choices":["Môj","Moja","Moje"]},
        {"id":"g2_auto","sk":"Moje auto je staré.","en":"My car is old.","blank":"Moje","choices":["Môj","Moja","Moje"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g3",
      "stage": "grammar",
      "title": "Present tense · What I do",
      "intro": "Good news: <b>every \"I\" form ends in -m</b> (except <i>som</i>). Verbs follow three main patterns, and only the vowel changes:<table><tr><th></th><th>volať (call)</th><th>robiť (do)</th><th>písať (write)</th></tr><tr><td>ja</td><td>volá<b>m</b></td><td>robí<b>m</b></td><td>píše<b>m</b></td></tr><tr><td>ty</td><td>volá<b>š</b></td><td>robí<b>š</b></td><td>píše<b>š</b></td></tr><tr><td>on/ona</td><td>volá</td><td>robí</td><td>píše</td></tr><tr><td>my</td><td>volá<b>me</b></td><td>robí<b>me</b></td><td>píše<b>me</b></td></tr><tr><td>vy</td><td>volá<b>te</b></td><td>robí<b>te</b></td><td>píše<b>te</b></td></tr><tr><td>oni</td><td>volajú</td><td>robia</td><td>píšu</td></tr></table>",
      "items": [
        {"id":"g3_volam","sk":"Volám mamu.","en":"I'm calling mom.","blank":"Volám","choices":["Volám","Voláš","Volá"]},
        {"id":"g3_robis","sk":"Čo robíš?","en":"What are you doing? (informal)","blank":"robíš","choices":["robím","robíš","robí"]},
        {"id":"g3_robim","sk":"Robím večeru.","en":"I'm making dinner.","blank":"Robím","choices":["Robím","Robíš","Robí"]},
        {"id":"g3_hovoris","sk":"Hovoríš po slovensky?","en":"Do you speak Slovak? (informal)","blank":"Hovoríš","choices":["Hovorím","Hovoríš","Hovorí"]},
        {"id":"g3_pisem","sk":"Píšem správu.","en":"I'm writing a message.","blank":"Píšem","choices":["Píšem","Píšeš","Píše"]},
        {"id":"g3_byvame","sk":"Bývame spolu.","en":"We live together.","blank":"Bývame","choices":["Bývam","Bývame","Bývajú"]},
        {"id":"g3_pracujem","sk":"Pracujem v nemocnici.","en":"I work in a hospital.","blank":"Pracujem","choices":["Pracujem","Pracuješ","Pracuje"]},
        {"id":"g3_rozumies","sk":"Rozumieš mi?","en":"Do you understand me? (informal)","blank":"Rozumieš","choices":["Rozumiem","Rozumieš","Rozumie"]},
        {"id":"g3_chces","sk":"Čo chceš robiť?","en":"What do you want to do? (informal)","blank":"chceš","choices":["chcem","chceš","chce"],"note":"chcieť (to want) is irregular: chcem, chceš, chce, chceme, chcete, chcú."},
        {"id":"g3_idem","sk":"Idem domov.","en":"I'm going home.","blank":"Idem","choices":["Idem","Ideš","Ide"]},
        {"id":"g3_hraju","sk":"Deti sa hrajú.","en":"The children are playing.","blank":"hrajú","choices":["hrá","hráme","hrajú"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g4",
      "stage": "grammar",
      "title": "I want, I have, I see",
      "intro": "This is your first real case, the <b>accusative</b>. When a noun is the thing you want, have or see, its ending can change:<table><tr><td><span class=\"g g-f\">f</span></td><td>-a → <b>-u</b></td><td>káva → Chcem káv<b>u</b>.</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"g g-m\">m</span> person or animal</td><td>+ <b>-a</b></td><td>brat → Mám brat<b>a</b>.</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"g g-m\">m</span> thing</td><td>no change</td><td>Chcem čaj.</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"g g-n\">n</span></td><td>no change</td><td>Chcem pivo.</td></tr></table>\"That\" changes too: <b>tá</b> žena → Vidím <b>tú</b> ženu.",
      "items": [
        {"id":"g4_vodu","sk":"Chcem vodu.","en":"I want water.","blank":"vodu","choices":["voda","vodu","vody"]},
        {"id":"g4_sestru","sk":"Mám sestru.","en":"I have a sister.","blank":"sestru","choices":["sestra","sestru","sestre"]},
        {"id":"g4_brata","sk":"Mám brata.","en":"I have a brother.","blank":"brata","choices":["brat","brata","bratovi"]},
        {"id":"g4_psa","sk":"Vidím psa.","en":"I see a dog.","blank":"psa","choices":["pes","psa","psovi"],"note":"pes → psa: the e drops out. A few short words do this."},
        {"id":"g4_caj","sk":"Pijem čaj.","en":"I'm drinking tea.","blank":"čaj","choices":["čaj","čaju","čaja"]},
        {"id":"g4_pivo","sk":"Chcem pivo.","en":"I want a beer.","blank":"pivo","choices":["pivo","pivu","piva"]},
        {"id":"g4_petra","sk":"Poznáš Petra?","en":"Do you know Peter? (informal)","blank":"Petra","choices":["Peter","Petra","Petrovi"]},
        {"id":"g4_kluc","sk":"Hľadám kľúč.","en":"I'm looking for the key.","blank":"kľúč","choices":["kľúč","kľúča","kľúču"]},
        {"id":"g4_otazku","sk":"Mám otázku.","en":"I have a question.","blank":"otázku","choices":["otázka","otázku","otázke"]},
        {"id":"g4_polievku","sk":"Mám rada polievku.","en":"I like soup. (woman)","blank":"polievku","choices":["polievka","polievku","polievke"]},
        {"id":"g4_zenu","sk":"Vidíš tú ženu?","en":"Do you see that woman? (informal)","blank":"tú ženu","choices":["tá žena","tú ženu","tej žene"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g5",
      "stage": "grammar",
      "title": "Past tense · What I did",
      "intro": "One of the easiest parts of Slovak. Take the infinitive, drop <b>-ť</b>, and add an ending for gender:<table><tr><td>robiť →</td><td>robi<b>l</b> (he)</td><td>robi<b>la</b> (she)</td><td>robi<b>li</b> (they)</td></tr></table>For \"I\" and \"you\", add <b>som</b> / <b>si</b>: <b>Robila som</b> = I did (said by a woman), <b>Robil som</b> = I did (said by a man). For \"we\" and \"you (formal)\", add <b>sme</b> / <b>ste</b> with the -li form.",
      "items": [
        {"id":"g5_bola","sk":"Bola som doma.","en":"I was at home. (woman)","blank":"Bola","choices":["Bol","Bola","Boli"]},
        {"id":"g5_pracovala","sk":"Včera som pracovala.","en":"Yesterday I worked. (woman)","blank":"pracovala","choices":["pracoval","pracovala","pracovali"]},
        {"id":"g5_robil","sk":"Čo si robil?","en":"What did you do? (to a man)","blank":"robil","choices":["robil","robila","robili"]},
        {"id":"g5_spala","sk":"Spala som dobre.","en":"I slept well. (woman)","blank":"Spala","choices":["Spal","Spala","Spali"]},
        {"id":"g5_videla","sk":"Videla som film.","en":"I saw a movie. (woman)","blank":"Videla","choices":["Videl","Videla","Videli"]},
        {"id":"g5_bol","sk":"Kde si bol?","en":"Where were you? (to a man)","blank":"bol","choices":["bol","bola","boli"]},
        {"id":"g5_varila","sk":"Mama varila obed.","en":"Mom cooked lunch.","blank":"varila","choices":["varil","varila","varili"]},
        {"id":"g5_boli","sk":"Boli sme v Tatrách.","en":"We were in the Tatras.","blank":"Boli","choices":["Bol","Bola","Boli"]},
        {"id":"g5_zabudla","sk":"Zabudla som.","en":"I forgot. (woman)","blank":"Zabudla","choices":["Zabudol","Zabudla","Zabudli"]},
        {"id":"g5_jedli","sk":"Jedli ste už?","en":"Have you eaten yet? (formal)","blank":"Jedli","choices":["Jedol","Jedla","Jedli"],"note":"jesť (to eat) is irregular: jedol, jedla, jedli."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g6",
      "stage": "grammar",
      "title": "Where? · v, na",
      "intro": "After <b>v</b> (in) and <b>na</b> (on / at), place names change their ending, usually to <b>-e</b> or <b>-i</b>:<table><tr><td>Bratislava</td><td>→ v Bratislav<b>e</b></td></tr><tr><td>obchod</td><td>→ v obchod<b>e</b></td></tr><tr><td>práca</td><td>→ v prác<b>i</b></td></tr><tr><td>letisko</td><td>→ na letisk<b>u</b></td></tr></table>Some places use <b>na</b> instead of v, which you just have to learn: <b>na stanici</b>, <b>na letisku</b>, and <b>na Slovensku</b> (but <i>v Amerike</i>).",
      "items": [
        {"id":"g6_praci","sk":"Som v práci.","en":"I'm at work.","blank":"práci","choices":["práca","práci","prácu"]},
        {"id":"g6_bratislave","sk":"Bývam v Bratislave.","en":"I live in Bratislava.","blank":"Bratislave","choices":["Bratislava","Bratislave","Bratislavu"]},
        {"id":"g6_obchode","sk":"Sme v obchode.","en":"We're in the shop.","blank":"obchode","choices":["obchod","obchode","obchodu"]},
        {"id":"g6_skole","sk":"Je v škole.","en":"He / she is at school.","blank":"škole","choices":["škola","škole","školu"]},
        {"id":"g6_stanici","sk":"Čakám na stanici.","en":"I'm waiting at the station.","blank":"stanici","choices":["stanica","stanici","stanicu"]},
        {"id":"g6_stole","sk":"Kľúč je na stole.","en":"The key is on the table.","blank":"stole","choices":["stôl","stole","stola"]},
        {"id":"g6_slovensku","sk":"Bola som na Slovensku.","en":"I was in Slovakia. (woman)","blank":"na Slovensku","choices":["na Slovensku","v Slovensku","na Slovensko"]},
        {"id":"g6_amerike","sk":"Žijem v Amerike.","en":"I live in America.","blank":"Amerike","choices":["Amerika","Amerike","Ameriku"]},
        {"id":"g6_namesti","sk":"Lekáreň je na námestí.","en":"The pharmacy is on the square.","blank":"námestí","choices":["námestie","námestí","námestiu"]},
        {"id":"g6_letisku","sk":"Sme na letisku.","en":"We're at the airport.","blank":"letisku","choices":["letisko","letisku","letiska"]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g7",
      "stage": "grammar",
      "title": "Questions & saying no",
      "intro": "To say \"don't\", glue <b>ne-</b> onto the front of the verb: <i>mám</i> → <b>nemám</b>, <i>chcem</i> → <b>nechcem</b>. The only exception is <i>byť</i>: <b>nie som</b>, <b>nie je</b>. For a yes/no question, keep the same words and raise your voice at the end: <b>Máš čas?</b>",
      "items": [
        {"id":"g7_co","sk":"čo","en":"what"},
        {"id":"g7_kto","sk":"kto","en":"who"},
        {"id":"g7_kde","sk":"kde","en":"where"},
        {"id":"g7_kedy","sk":"kedy","en":"when"},
        {"id":"g7_preco","sk":"prečo","en":"why"},
        {"id":"g7_ako","sk":"ako","en":"how"},
        {"id":"g7_nemam","sk":"Nemám čas.","en":"I don't have time.","blank":"Nemám","choices":["Nemám","Nie mám","Mám nie"]},
        {"id":"g7_nechcem","sk":"Nechcem.","en":"I don't want to.","blank":"Nechcem","choices":["Nechcem","Nie chcem","Chcem nie"]},
        {"id":"g7_nepijem","sk":"Nepijem alkohol.","en":"I don't drink alcohol.","blank":"Nepijem","choices":["Nepijem","Nie pijem","Pijem nie"]},
        {"id":"g7_precnie","sk":"Prečo nie?","en":"Why not?"},
        {"id":"g7_kedy2","sk":"Kedy prídeš?","en":"When are you coming? (informal)"},
        {"id":"g7_kto2","sk":"Kto je to?","en":"Who is that?"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g8",
      "stage": "grammar",
      "title": "Want, can, must",
      "intro": "Three helper verbs plus a second verb in the <b>-ť</b> form (the infinitive):<table><tr><td>chcieť</td><td><b>Chcem</b> ísť.</td><td>I want to go.</td></tr><tr><td>môcť</td><td><b>Môžem</b> ísť.</td><td>I can go.</td></tr><tr><td>musieť</td><td><b>Musím</b> ísť.</td><td>I have to go.</td></tr><tr><td>vedieť</td><td><b>Viem</b> variť.</td><td>I know how to cook.</td></tr></table>",
      "items": [
        {"id":"g8_chcem","sk":"Chcem ísť domov.","en":"I want to go home.","blank":"Chcem","choices":["Chcem","Chceš","Chce"]},
        {"id":"g8_mozem","sk":"Môžem ti pomôcť?","en":"Can I help you? (informal)","blank":"Môžem","choices":["Môžem","Môžeš","Môže"]},
        {"id":"g8_musim","sk":"Musím ísť.","en":"I have to go.","blank":"Musím","choices":["Musím","Musíš","Musí"]},
        {"id":"g8_musis","sk":"Musíš to skúsiť.","en":"You have to try it. (informal)","blank":"Musíš","choices":["Musím","Musíš","Musí"]},
        {"id":"g8_mozete","sk":"Môžete mi pomôcť?","en":"Can you help me? (formal)","blank":"Môžete","choices":["Môžeme","Môžete","Môžu"]},
        {"id":"g8_chces","sk":"Chceš ísť von?","en":"Do you want to go out? (informal)","blank":"Chceš","choices":["Chcem","Chceš","Chce"]},
        {"id":"g8_nemozem","sk":"Nemôžem spať.","en":"I can't sleep.","blank":"Nemôžem","choices":["Nemôžem","Nie môžem","Môžem nie"]},
        {"id":"g8_viem","sk":"Viem variť.","en":"I know how to cook.","blank":"Viem","choices":["Viem","Vieš","Vie"],"note":"Use vedieť (not môcť) for skills: Viem plávať = I can swim."},
        {"id":"g8_mozem2","sk":"Môžem?","en":"May I?"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m1",
      "stage": "clinic",
      "title": "Lekárka · At the hospital",
      "intro": "In Slovak healthcare, always use <b>vy</b> with patients and address them as <b>pán</b> / <b>pani</b> + surname. Female surnames end in <b>-ová</b> or <b>-á</b>: <i>pán Novák</i>, <i>pani Nováková</i>. Job titles have feminine forms, so you are a <b>lekárka</b> and a <b>psychiatrička</b>.",
      "items": [
        {"id":"m1_lekarka","sk":"lekárka","en":"doctor (woman)","g":"f","note":"A male doctor is lekár."},
        {"id":"m1_psychiatricka","sk":"psychiatrička","en":"psychiatrist (woman)","g":"f","note":"A male psychiatrist is psychiater."},
        {"id":"m1_psycholog","sk":"psychológ","en":"psychologist","g":"m"},
        {"id":"m1_sestra","sk":"zdravotná sestra","en":"nurse","g":"f","note":"Usually just sestra, the same word as \"sister\"."},
        {"id":"m1_pacient","sk":"pacient","en":"patient (man)","g":"m"},
        {"id":"m1_pacientka","sk":"pacientka","en":"patient (woman)","g":"f"},
        {"id":"m1_nemocnica","sk":"nemocnica","en":"hospital","g":"f"},
        {"id":"m1_ambulancia","sk":"ambulancia","en":"outpatient clinic","g":"f"},
        {"id":"m1_oddelenie","sk":"oddelenie","en":"ward / department","g":"n"},
        {"id":"m1_liek","sk":"liek","en":"medication","g":"m"},
        {"id":"m1_recept","sk":"recept","en":"prescription","g":"m","note":"Also means \"recipe\"."},
        {"id":"m1_diagnoza","sk":"diagnóza","en":"diagnosis","g":"f"},
        {"id":"m1_vysetrenie","sk":"vyšetrenie","en":"examination","g":"n"},
        {"id":"m1_somlekarka","sk":"Som psychiatrička.","en":"I'm a psychiatrist. (woman)"},
        {"id":"m1_nechsapaci","sk":"Pani Nováková, nech sa páči.","en":"Mrs. Nováková, please come in.","note":"Nech sa páči: \"please, go ahead / come in / here you are\"."},
        {"id":"m1_posadte","sk":"Posaďte sa, prosím.","en":"Please sit down."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m2",
      "stage": "clinic",
      "title": "The first conversation",
      "intro": "Opening an interview. These are all formal (<b>vy</b>) questions. Notice the endings: <b>-te</b> marks the formal \"you\" in verbs, like <i>cítite</i>, <i>prichádzate</i>, <i>rozumiete</i>.",
      "items": [
        {"id":"m2_scim","sk":"S čím prichádzate?","en":"What brings you in?","note":"Literally \"What are you coming with?\". The standard opener in Slovak clinics."},
        {"id":"m2_trapi","sk":"Čo vás trápi?","en":"What's troubling you?"},
        {"id":"m2_citite","sk":"Ako sa cítite?","en":"How are you feeling?"},
        {"id":"m2_akodlho","sk":"Ako dlho to trvá?","en":"How long has this been going on?"},
        {"id":"m2_kedyzacalo","sk":"Kedy to začalo?","en":"When did it start?"},
        {"id":"m2_porozpravajte","sk":"Porozprávajte mi o tom.","en":"Tell me about it."},
        {"id":"m2_neponahlajte","sk":"Nemusíte sa ponáhľať.","en":"There's no need to rush."},
        {"id":"m2_doverne","sk":"Všetko, čo poviete, je dôverné.","en":"Everything you say is confidential."},
        {"id":"m2_rozumiemvam","sk":"Rozumiem vám.","en":"I understand you."},
        {"id":"m2_tazke","sk":"To musí byť ťažké.","en":"That must be hard."},
        {"id":"m2_rozumiete","sk":"Rozumiete mi?","en":"Do you understand me? (formal)"},
        {"id":"m2_pomalsie","sk":"Môžete hovoriť pomalšie?","en":"Could you speak more slowly?"},
        {"id":"m2_tlmocnik","sk":"Potrebujeme tlmočníka.","en":"We need an interpreter."}
      ]
